// Large number literals of every element type (#3457): packed by the parser (16 elements or
// more), stored as one block of read-only data when a module constant, and built by a local
// literal. Each table is read by length, by index (first, an inner one, last) and by `for…of`;
// the values (maximums, byte patterns such as 0x0102030405060708) show a wrong width or byte
// order. The f32 table rounds `0.1` once, as a Float32Array does.

